1
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:20,770
[foreboding music playing]

2
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:23,565
[all chanting]

3
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:50,675
[suspenseful music playing]

4
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:43,978
[shaky breathing]

5
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:48,316
[retches]

6
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:53,822
[gasps]

7
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,536
[breathes heavily]

8
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:08,128
[pants heavily]

9
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,757
[sighs wearily]

10
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:22,517
[rumbling]

11
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,353
[all gasp]

12
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:38,908
[dramatic sting]

13
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:41,828
[wheezing]

14
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:49,252
[grunts]

15
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:00,638
[knife scrapes]

16
00:03:05,059 --> 00:03:05,894
[Javier] Ramon.

17
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:08,479
You packed Dad's weapons, right?

18
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:15,445
- [woman screams] Stop!
- [gasps]

19
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:17,488
[woman sobbing]

20
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:18,406
No!

21
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,158
[gasps]

22
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:21,075
[screams] Lay off!

23
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,328
Fuck! Let her go!

24
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,665
[suspenseful music playing]

25
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,834
[Javier breathing heavily]

26
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,756
Ramon, what are we gonna do?

27
00:03:34,839 --> 00:03:37,133
[breathing heavily]

28
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:40,553
Run! Now!

29
00:03:42,096 --> 00:03:43,348
[Javier] Rafael! Hey!

30
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:46,601
- Andres!
- Wait, wait!

31
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:48,394
Come on. Come on.

32
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,687
[Andres] Hurry up. Let's go.

33
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:55,526
[all panting]

34
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:10,291
- [bone creaks]
- [all gasping]

35
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:11,668
[whimpers]

36
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:34,816
- [thumping]
- [all gasp]

37
00:04:36,609 --> 00:04:37,610
[branch breaks]

38
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:42,115
[all groaning, panting]

39
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,536
- [yelps]
- [gasps]

40
00:04:46,619 --> 00:04:48,037
[all gasping, panting]

41
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:50,957
Captain! Captain!

42
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:52,417
No! Wait!

43
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,334
Stop! Let me go!

44
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:54,752
[Ramon] Forget him. Just come on.

45
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:56,170
Come on, come on.

46
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:57,171
Go!

47
00:04:57,255 --> 00:04:58,631
- No, wait!
- [grunts]

48
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:03,553
[suspenseful music playing]

49
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:10,351
- [Tessa] Who could that--
- [screaming]

50
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:12,270
- [both screaming]
- [Andres] Javier!

51
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:17,650
- Javier!
- No! No!

52
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:20,653
[screaming]

53
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:23,197
- What are you doing?
- [pants]

54
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:26,784
The captain was taken by that one.

55
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:28,328
They also took Violeta.

56
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,662
It's kill or be killed,

57
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:32,623
if you want to survive.

58
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,378
[bird hooting]

59
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:45,470
[Ramon] Javier.

60
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,394
We'll get you all fixed up
when we get home.

61
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:55,563
Doesn't look that bad.

62
00:05:55,646 --> 00:05:57,565
Easy for you to say, Andres.

63
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:07,366
[Tessa breathing heavily]

64
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:18,961
Tessa.

65
00:06:19,837 --> 00:06:20,671
[breathing stops]

66
00:06:22,381 --> 00:06:25,676
Ramon, we knew
she was never going to make it.

67
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:31,682
The same thing will happen to us
unless we get out of here.

68
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:33,559
[Rafael] There was no way
she could have survived.

69
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:34,977
I don't want to end up like her.

70
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:37,396
We have nothing to eat.

71
00:06:38,564 --> 00:06:41,150
Maybe we shouldn't waste the flesh.

72
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:43,402
What are you saying?

73
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:47,490
Huh?

74
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:50,118
You lost your mind? Hey?

75
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:56,207
- I think Rafael's right.
- What? You as well now?

76
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,876
You want to ask the locals for help?

77
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,796
We have nothing to eat here
and no actual plan.

78
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:02,797
[gasps] Fuck!

79
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:06,134
[grunting]

80
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:13,057
[growls]

81
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:15,643
[screams] No!

82
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:18,521
[gasps]

83
00:07:18,604 --> 00:07:19,522
Ramon!

84
00:07:19,605 --> 00:07:21,149
Ramon! Ramon!

85
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:25,862
[gasping]

86
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:28,406
[Javier] Oh, shit. What the fuck is that?

87
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:32,326
[Javier screams, pants]

88
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:46,549
[footsteps receding]

89
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:49,635
[mysterious music playing]

90
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:58,561
[thunder rumbling]

91
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:15,328
[Ramon] <i>"And I say that the things</i>
<i>which the gentiles sacrifice…</i>

92
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:20,958
<i>are to the devil and not to God."</i>

93
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:22,543
[thunder rumbling]

94
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,925
[man groaning]

95
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,061
[Ramon] <i>"And I say that ye shall not…"</i>

96
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:43,439
[man screams]

97
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,691
[pants]

98
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:48,819
[Ramon] <i>"…have fellowship with devils."</i>

99
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:53,491
[man grunts, pants]

100
00:08:58,246 --> 00:08:59,372
"I say he cannot

101
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:02,416
drink from the cup of the Lord,

102
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,627
and also from that…

103
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:08,714
of devils."

104
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:15,388
<i>"And neither shall ye be part acres</i>
<i>at the Lord's table…</i>

105
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:21,018
<i>and at the table of devils."</i>

106
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:23,062
[snarls]

107
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:36,659
[panting]

108
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:37,618
[sighs in relief]

109
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:40,788
[thunder rumbling]

110
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:42,790
[Ramon] "Let every man seek the wealth

111
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:47,461
or another."

112
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,969
[glorious music playing]

113
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:02,310
[opening theme music playing]

114
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:08,542
BALARAW: BLOOD ISLAND

115
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:13,047
[woman groans]

116
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:18,761
[grunts]

117
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:20,554
[panting]

118
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:35,903
[groans]

119
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:40,116
[pants]

120
00:11:50,459 --> 00:11:51,419
Here, use this.

121
00:11:56,006 --> 00:11:57,591
[Sabina grunts]

122
00:11:57,675 --> 00:11:59,468
[gentle waves crashing]

123
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:07,476
[Vedasto] Rebecca.

124
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,105
Rebecca?

125
00:12:25,536 --> 00:12:26,787
You're making that face.

126
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:30,166
You're making that face, too.

127
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:33,502
I get worried when you do.

128
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:37,590
I didn't keep anything from Mama or Papa.

129
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:39,842
After they've gone,

130
00:12:39,925 --> 00:12:41,886
seeing their things always made me cry.

131
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:43,929
I get upset even now.

132
00:12:50,686 --> 00:12:52,062
It's just us two, now.

133
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,069
It was wrong not to take anything.

134
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,576
Vedasto, what are you doing?

135
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:06,494
[sighs]

136
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:11,874
Oh, I'm fine. I don't need it.

137
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:15,503
- Don't worry.
- Mm-hm.

138
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:20,758
[both chuckle]

139
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:22,384
Okay?

140
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,345
It's just to stop you crying.

141
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:26,138
When you're asleep, I'll take it back.

142
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,848
- [Vedasto chuckles]
- [sighs]

143
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:33,395
I honestly don't get your obsession
with Babang Yawa,

144
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:36,106
the Bermuda Triangle of the Philippines.

145
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,816
Even the Bermuda Triangle,

146
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,777
that's been well
and truly debunked, you know?

147
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,946
And ours isn't real.

148
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:43,113
Ours is a fake.

149
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:46,408
There's proof of it, all right?

150
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:48,536
There are conspiracy theories.

151
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:51,705
You came along, though.

152
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:57,586
[Jonas] Ah, shit!

153
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,381
Yeah, shit. Jonas!

154
00:14:00,965 --> 00:14:02,466
- [Jonas] Damn it!
- [Ding] You said it!

155
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:04,176
Stop the boat! It's over there!

156
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:09,515
Leave it to me.

157
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:13,561
Be careful out there!

158
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,146
Rebecca.

159
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:17,064
Let's do this now.

160
00:14:17,147 --> 00:14:18,274
It's too dangerous.

161
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:19,191
Becca?

162
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:21,235
- [groans]
- [Vedasto] Becca!

163
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,030
You be careful.

164
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:28,701
You hear me?

165
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,874
[pants]

166
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:37,209
[Vedasto] Just grab it and swim back here!

167
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:42,631
- It's over there!
- Where?

168
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:45,551
[Brian] It's getting rough.

169
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:47,094
The waves are building.

170
00:14:47,177 --> 00:14:48,554
[Vedasto] Hurry, Rebecca!

171
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:51,265
[pants]

172
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:57,771
[Vedasto] Come on, you got it.
Now get back here quickly!

173
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,649
- Rebecca, hurry!
- Oh, yeah!

174
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,318
[men cheering]

175
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:08,115
[Vedasto] Rebecca, watch out!

176
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:09,408
There's a wave coming!

177
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,578
Swim back now, quickly!

178
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:17,333
What? [gasps]

179
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,379
[Vedasto] Swim back! Swim!

180
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:27,718
[panting]

181
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:33,057
[suspenseful music playing]

182
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:40,064
Hey.

183
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:47,988
Vedasto!

184
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:49,740
Hey!

185
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:53,827
[panting]

186
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:59,375
[wind howling]

187
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:09,176
[breathes heavily]

188
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:35,369
[muffled sinister music playing]

189
00:16:58,017 --> 00:16:59,018
[coughing]

190
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:04,523
[gasps]

191
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:08,527
[coughing]

192
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:33,218
[mysterious music playing]

193
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,399
Vedasto?

194
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:51,612
[pants]

195
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:00,913
Vedasto?

196
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:09,213
Vedasto!

197
00:18:25,395 --> 00:18:28,357
[suspenseful music playing]

198
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:51,213
[gasps]

199
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:01,265
[gasps]

200
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:02,933
[low growl]

201
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,401
[gasps]

202
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:13,402
[low growl]

203
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:15,779
[body thuds]

204
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:19,700
[whimpering]

205
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,949
[suspenseful music playing]

206
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:06,079
Vedasto?

207
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:10,083
Vedasto…

208
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:33,065
[snores softly]

209
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:49,081
[suspenseful music continues]

210
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:14,481
[Ramon] Who's the president now?

211
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:17,401
- I doubt you'd be able to work it out.
- Mmm.

212
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:19,069
Okay, I'll give you a clue.

213
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:19,987
Mmm.

214
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:21,405
It's an entertainer.

215
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:23,240
[chuckles]

216
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:25,158
I don't even want to try.

217
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:26,535
[men laughing]

218
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:27,661
[Rebecca] Vedasto?

219
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:28,578
[Vedasto] Becca!

220
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,960
[Ding] Becca, let's eat.

221
00:21:37,212 --> 00:21:38,046
Good idea.

222
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:39,506
Sit here.

223
00:21:40,507 --> 00:21:41,800
Rebecca, this is Señor Ramon.

224
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:44,094
Just Ramon.

225
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:45,262
She your sister?

226
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:46,179
My youngest.

227
00:21:47,681 --> 00:21:49,474
Rebecca, Mr. Ramon.

228
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:51,351
Ramon Cardoma.

229
00:21:53,937 --> 00:21:55,814
Sit down, please.

230
00:21:57,899 --> 00:21:59,401
Diwa, bring up more food.

231
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:04,740
- [footsteps receding]
- [wooden floor creaking]

232
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:09,036
Where are we, Señor Ramon?

233
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,246
We're on Balaraw.

234
00:22:12,372 --> 00:22:13,373
I've never heard of it.

235
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,834
It's shaped like a dagger.

236
00:22:16,793 --> 00:22:18,170
So that's what the locals named it.

237
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:20,672
I didn't notice.

238
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:24,676
If you're here for much longer, you will.

239
00:22:25,218 --> 00:22:26,470
We won't be staying.

240
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,181
[chuckles]

241
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:30,474
How long have you been here?

242
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:34,811
It was something like, two years ago.

243
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:38,065
We decided to stay for good.

244
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:40,859
[Rebecca] But… don't you all want to…

245
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:43,612
go back to Manila?

246
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:45,447
[scoffs]

247
00:22:46,281 --> 00:22:47,824
We have nothing to go back to.

248
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:50,452
Balaraw is our home now.

249
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:53,371
You're on the run, are you? [chuckles]

250
00:22:53,997 --> 00:22:56,041
- Are you in debt?
- Yeah, loan sharks.

251
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:58,043
[men laughing]

252
00:23:00,337 --> 00:23:01,338
My brothers and I,

253
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:04,591
and Diwa, and Crisanto,

254
00:23:04,674 --> 00:23:06,676
all of us, this is our home.

255
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:09,930
This is our island now.

256
00:23:10,639 --> 00:23:11,556
[Andres] Yeah.

257
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,974
It wasn't a first choice,

258
00:23:14,434 --> 00:23:15,560
but we got used to it.

259
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:18,271
- [footsteps approaching]
- [wooden floor creaking]

260
00:23:18,355 --> 00:23:20,273
The world outside was in chaos

261
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:21,358
- when we left.
- Thank you.

262
00:23:21,441 --> 00:23:23,735
- [Vedasto] Yes. Thank you.
- That's not any better than here.

263
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:26,780
- [footsteps]
- [wooden floor creaking]

264
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:27,697
[Ramon] Rebecca.

265
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:30,408
Eat.

266
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,328
[fork scrapes]

267
00:23:39,084 --> 00:23:40,418
When I was in the jungle…

268
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:45,132
I think I saw a person.

269
00:23:47,592 --> 00:23:48,760
A person, though…

270
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:50,178
[groans]

271
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:53,265
They had huge wings,

272
00:23:54,015 --> 00:23:55,392
like a gigantic bat.

273
00:23:58,436 --> 00:24:01,148
I'm not sure if I remember correctly, but…

274
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:05,193
Sorry. I'm…

275
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:07,404
It sounds absurd.

276
00:24:07,946 --> 00:24:08,947
I'm probably tired.

277
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:12,242
It's not absurd.

278
00:24:14,536 --> 00:24:15,912
Come with me when you've finished eating.

279
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:19,666
I can eat later.

280
00:24:23,587 --> 00:24:24,421
Are you sure?

281
00:24:25,338 --> 00:24:26,173
Then, let's go.

282
00:24:32,762 --> 00:24:34,890
This is Rafael, our eldest brother.

283
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:38,435
He's the doctor I was talking about.

284
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:41,938
My brother is the only doctor we have.

285
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:44,608
Dr. Vedasto Tejeros.

286
00:24:45,942 --> 00:24:47,652
But I'm not that kind of doctor.

287
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:50,488
[groans]

288
00:24:51,781 --> 00:24:53,909
She's asking about the, uh,

289
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:55,535
the creature.

290
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:57,913
She wants to see it.

291
00:25:05,462 --> 00:25:06,838
- Wait, Ramon.
- [Vedasto] Go on then.

292
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:07,797
Ramon, wait.

293
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:09,549
- Should I go as well?
- Ramon.

294
00:25:12,510 --> 00:25:13,345
This one's dead.

295
00:25:15,555 --> 00:25:17,349
It died around a week ago.

296
00:25:20,769 --> 00:25:22,604
Is this what you saw?

297
00:25:25,523 --> 00:25:26,358
Mm-hm.

298
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:32,364
This is the last of its kind
here on Balaraw.

299
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:36,910
[mysterious music playing]

300
00:25:38,161 --> 00:25:39,496
If this is the last…

301
00:25:41,998 --> 00:25:43,250
what was it that I saw?

302
00:25:45,835 --> 00:25:48,421
Maybe this island
was trying to talk to you.

303
00:25:58,431 --> 00:25:59,432
Will you let me touch it?

304
00:26:09,067 --> 00:26:12,028
[breathing heavily]

305
00:26:48,648 --> 00:26:51,151
[calm music playing]

306
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:31,441
There's something different
about the soil here.

307
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:37,989
This is really sticky,
like it's got sap in it.

308
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:39,157
Do you mind if we get a sample?

309
00:27:39,741 --> 00:27:41,659
We can study it when we get back home.

310
00:27:42,744 --> 00:27:43,620
Be my guest.

311
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:49,125
[Ding] Has our boat been found?

312
00:27:52,587 --> 00:27:54,631
They're still looking but don't worry.

313
00:27:54,714 --> 00:27:58,051
We can assist you
if there's anything at all wrong with it.

314
00:27:58,134 --> 00:28:00,220
Javier is an excellent engineer.

315
00:28:01,679 --> 00:28:02,931
I could help, too.

316
00:28:20,573 --> 00:28:22,826
[Ramon] So you're the bravest
amongst you, hm?

317
00:28:22,909 --> 00:28:24,369
You're the one who got the camera.

318
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:26,663
- [Rebecca] Oh, well.
- [Ramon chuckles]

319
00:28:26,746 --> 00:28:29,416
- [Rebecca] You know, I'm a strong swimmer.
- [both chuckling]

320
00:28:29,499 --> 00:28:31,334
[crickets chirping]

321
00:28:38,091 --> 00:28:40,635
You know, my brother
doesn't believe in Babang Yawa.

322
00:28:43,054 --> 00:28:44,389
Is your brother religious?

323
00:28:45,348 --> 00:28:46,850
Ah-- [chuckles]

324
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:48,893
- What is it?
- [laughs]

325
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:50,895
No, the opposite.

326
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:55,775
He hasn't had faith in any God
since we were young.

327
00:28:57,152 --> 00:28:58,903
That was my mother's cross to bear.

328
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:02,115
She was a very strict Catholic.

329
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:05,535
[scoffs] I see.

330
00:29:07,912 --> 00:29:09,497
My brother and I are the same,

331
00:29:10,039 --> 00:29:13,001
but I just didn't tell my mother.

332
00:29:15,628 --> 00:29:17,505
Yet you believe in Babang Yawa.

333
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:22,761
There has to be a scientific
explanation, though,

334
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:25,972
as to why a lot of ships
get shipwrecked here.

335
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:28,892
Yours.

336
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:29,893
Ours.

337
00:29:31,186 --> 00:29:32,228
I guess it's--

338
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:33,354
Yeah, but…

339
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:36,941
We were on an airplane.

340
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:38,985
A plane?

341
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:45,700
Here we are.

342
00:29:46,659 --> 00:29:47,577
Oh, wow.

343
00:29:49,662 --> 00:29:50,830
It's gorgeous.

344
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:57,045
What?

345
00:29:58,087 --> 00:29:59,756
[chuckles]

346
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:05,470
Come on.

347
00:30:06,971 --> 00:30:07,931
Yes. [chuckles]

348
00:30:09,390 --> 00:30:10,600
Careful now.

349
00:30:13,311 --> 00:30:14,145
- [yelps]
- Oh!

350
00:30:31,704 --> 00:30:33,748
[crickets chirping]

351
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:33,516
[exhales sharply]

352
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:38,730
That's mine.

353
00:31:40,648 --> 00:31:41,482
Ah.

354
00:31:50,491 --> 00:31:52,118
I got it from Señor Rafael.

355
00:32:04,714 --> 00:32:06,049
Where did you get yours?

356
00:32:07,133 --> 00:32:08,051
My brother.

357
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:25,068
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

358
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:28,363
Catch me if you can!

359
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:29,739
- [laughs]
- Come get me.

360
00:32:29,822 --> 00:32:31,157
- [man laughs]
- [boy laughs]

361
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:32,909
- Think you can catch me?
- [boy] I'm gonna get you.

362
00:32:32,992 --> 00:32:34,494
- [laughter]
- You could do this.

363
00:32:35,787 --> 00:32:36,871
[Rebecca] Hm?

364
00:32:36,955 --> 00:32:40,208
[Jonas] It's like the soil
has kind of sap in it, right?

365
00:32:40,291 --> 00:32:42,794
You mustn't rush it
or you'll cut yourself.

366
00:32:43,336 --> 00:32:45,755
- Watch it--
- Rebecca! Vedasto!

367
00:32:45,838 --> 00:32:47,757
- Look what I got.
- [Vedasto] Does it work?

368
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:49,550
- [Ding] It was in my bag.
- Is it working?

369
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:50,551
[Ding] Of course it does.

370
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:52,595
Interesting. Get in the picture.

371
00:32:52,679 --> 00:32:53,763
- Come out.
- Here we go.

372
00:32:53,846 --> 00:32:55,974
- Okay, look over there. It's a camera.
- Stand close together.

373
00:32:56,057 --> 00:32:57,266
You ready?

374
00:32:57,350 --> 00:32:59,477
- One, two.
- Look over there.

375
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:01,437
- [Ding] Here we go.
- [camera clicks]

376
00:33:02,397 --> 00:33:04,190
Nice!

377
00:33:04,273 --> 00:33:05,358
Did it work?

378
00:33:05,441 --> 00:33:06,609
[Ding] You wanna see it?

379
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:09,320
And the picture hasn't come up yet.

380
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:12,365
[sighs] It's so hot.

381
00:33:13,741 --> 00:33:14,617
There.

382
00:33:14,701 --> 00:33:16,828
You're hot. [laughs]

383
00:33:16,911 --> 00:33:18,329
[Vedasto] It has a special surface

384
00:33:18,413 --> 00:33:20,540
and when the light hits it,
it creates a picture.

385
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:22,750
[Ding] There's not much film left.

386
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:25,878
- [Vedasto] How much left?
- [Ding] Only four.

387
00:33:25,962 --> 00:33:27,005
Hey, can you take this?

388
00:33:30,758 --> 00:33:32,051
You can keep it.

389
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:33,678
Look how well it's developed.

390
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:37,473
Ah. Look there.

391
00:34:10,214 --> 00:34:12,008
[woman] You're the one
who saw the creature?

392
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:15,136
I was.

393
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:17,513
What sort of creature is it?

394
00:34:20,099 --> 00:34:21,434
The brothers said nothing.

395
00:34:23,478 --> 00:34:24,312
[Rebecca] No, ma'am.

396
00:34:25,688 --> 00:34:27,732
But there was a dead one in their house.

397
00:34:31,235 --> 00:34:32,528
That's Talas.

398
00:34:32,612 --> 00:34:34,113
That's what it's called?

399
00:34:35,198 --> 00:34:36,240
I liked Talas.

400
00:34:36,991 --> 00:34:38,826
But he was a little reckless.

401
00:34:39,410 --> 00:34:41,829
He knew it was dangerous
to go out on his own.

402
00:34:43,164 --> 00:34:44,707
He? What do you mean?

403
00:34:44,791 --> 00:34:46,709
[woman] He went
to the other side of the island.

404
00:34:49,003 --> 00:34:50,296
There was an accident.

405
00:34:50,379 --> 00:34:51,380
He got injured.

406
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:53,424
And nobody knew.

407
00:34:54,050 --> 00:34:54,884
And then…

408
00:34:56,177 --> 00:34:57,345
he transformed.

409
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:00,181
Transformed?

410
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:05,561
Wait. Are you saying that
that thing in the house is human?

411
00:35:05,645 --> 00:35:06,938
Not anymore.

412
00:35:07,021 --> 00:35:10,108
If the wound isn't taken care of,
then we transform.

413
00:35:11,234 --> 00:35:14,445
The wound will heal,
but we're changed forever.

414
00:35:17,490 --> 00:35:19,158
What if one of you passes on?

415
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:20,535
It's no different.

416
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:23,204
But that hardly ever happens now.

417
00:35:24,705 --> 00:35:26,165
We know the cure now.

418
00:35:28,209 --> 00:35:29,127
Holy meat.

419
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:31,504
Meat?

420
00:35:32,213 --> 00:35:33,965
But there's no livestock here on Balaraw.

421
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:39,220
- [snickers]
- [suspenseful music playing]

422
00:35:41,806 --> 00:35:43,558
There's a lot of us around.

423
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:51,691
How is she?

424
00:35:54,610 --> 00:35:55,987
[Sabina] She'll be all right for now.

425
00:35:57,196 --> 00:35:58,781
But her wound is serious.

426
00:36:00,199 --> 00:36:01,742
It could get infected.

427
00:36:03,452 --> 00:36:06,080
Only the Cardomas can help her this time.

428
00:36:07,373 --> 00:36:08,749
Let's get off this island.

429
00:36:10,376 --> 00:36:11,544
Got a boat here?

430
00:36:18,467 --> 00:36:19,635
Where?

431
00:36:19,719 --> 00:36:20,636
At the beach.

432
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:23,222
Head right, out of the cave.

433
00:36:25,224 --> 00:36:26,934
It's near the shoreline.

434
00:36:27,018 --> 00:36:28,227
That's where I hid it.

435
00:36:31,355 --> 00:36:33,107
Why didn't you just leave this place?

436
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:35,860
I kept searching for you.

437
00:36:38,446 --> 00:36:39,655
You think I didn't try?

438
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:43,534
Is Ramon my real father?

439
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:47,580
[Ding] <i>Hold on.</i>

440
00:36:47,663 --> 00:36:51,042
Are you saying you were a millionaire

441
00:36:51,125 --> 00:36:52,919
and you lived in a mansion?

442
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:54,337
- Mm.
- Oh.

443
00:36:54,420 --> 00:36:56,047
- You're rich.
- Not just that.

444
00:36:56,547 --> 00:36:57,798
And your folks are connected.

445
00:36:57,882 --> 00:37:00,718
- He's a millionaire.
- Really well-connected.

446
00:37:00,801 --> 00:37:02,887
[men laughing]

447
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:04,847
Pour me another one.

448
00:37:04,931 --> 00:37:07,433
- And you turned your backs on all of this?
- [Jonas] No, no, no, next to you.

449
00:37:07,516 --> 00:37:08,726
Is that how it goes?

450
00:37:09,977 --> 00:37:11,562
You're crazy to do that.

451
00:37:11,646 --> 00:37:14,649
- [laughs]
- Hey, don't call it crazy.

452
00:37:14,732 --> 00:37:16,192
But look at what we have.

453
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:19,570
Well, it's your choice.

454
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:20,780
[sighs]

455
00:37:20,863 --> 00:37:23,115
Our airplane crashed here, Vedasto.

456
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:25,952
That's how we ended up here.

457
00:37:30,289 --> 00:37:31,457
You and I are different.

458
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,543
I have faith in the Holy Word.

459
00:37:35,503 --> 00:37:37,630
I don't have faith in accidents

460
00:37:39,465 --> 00:37:40,299
or chance.

461
00:37:41,801 --> 00:37:44,804
I believe that we were all
brought here by the Lord.

462
00:37:46,138 --> 00:37:48,266
And so I think all this occurred for…

463
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:50,726
a reason.

464
00:37:52,603 --> 00:37:54,522
And it's not for me to question that.

465
00:37:55,439 --> 00:37:56,565
Cheers, Don Ramon.

466
00:37:57,483 --> 00:37:58,943
- Hand me the bottle.
- [Ding] To Señor Ramon!

467
00:37:59,026 --> 00:38:00,444
Come on. Hand it over.

468
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:03,739
- [Vedasto] Cheers.
- [Ding] Glass half full, huh?

469
00:38:03,823 --> 00:38:07,034
- But you're here all alone.
- [Ding] When I become a millionaire,

470
00:38:07,118 --> 00:38:09,495
every day, I'm gonna eat bulalo.

471
00:38:09,578 --> 00:38:10,955
You know, all of you here,

472
00:38:11,038 --> 00:38:12,999
don't you ever get lonely by yourself?

473
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:14,834
[men laughing]

474
00:38:14,917 --> 00:38:16,168
Isn't that obvious?

475
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:17,878
You're full of "bull-alo."

476
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:21,590
[men laughing]

477
00:38:50,870 --> 00:38:51,704
Ramon?

478
00:39:01,088 --> 00:39:02,006
Ding?

479
00:39:02,089 --> 00:39:03,007
Brian!

480
00:39:03,966 --> 00:39:04,925
Vedasto!

481
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:07,178
[pants]

482
00:39:07,261 --> 00:39:10,264
[tense rhythmic music playing]

483
00:39:22,651 --> 00:39:23,652
Diwa?

484
00:39:25,821 --> 00:39:26,822
Diwa.

485
00:39:29,075 --> 00:39:30,326
Have you seen my brother?

486
00:39:31,535 --> 00:39:32,578
What about Señor Ramon?

487
00:39:35,456 --> 00:39:36,290
Where are they?

488
00:39:37,333 --> 00:39:38,584
Do you know?

489
00:39:40,836 --> 00:39:42,380
Diwa, you have to tell me.

490
00:39:42,463 --> 00:39:44,298
I need your help, Diwa.

491
00:39:46,092 --> 00:39:48,761
Tell me where they are! Please.

492
00:39:51,847 --> 00:39:53,307
[bird hooting]

493
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:02,024
No!

494
00:40:02,108 --> 00:40:03,401
- Please, have mercy.
- Get in!

495
00:40:03,484 --> 00:40:04,568
Come on!

496
00:40:04,652 --> 00:40:06,529
[Vedasto coughing]

497
00:40:08,114 --> 00:40:09,240
[punches landing]

498
00:40:12,118 --> 00:40:13,035
- [grunts]
- [groans]

499
00:40:14,745 --> 00:40:15,746
[grunts]

500
00:40:17,331 --> 00:40:19,083
[Vedasto wheezes, coughs]

501
00:40:27,842 --> 00:40:28,676
[grunts]

502
00:40:31,762 --> 00:40:33,973
- Vedasto!
- Don't struggle.

503
00:40:34,682 --> 00:40:36,308
- [Rebecca] Let me go!
- [Ramon] Don't fight me.

504
00:40:36,392 --> 00:40:38,686
- [Rebecca] Let go of me, you bastard!
- [Ramon] Calm down, Rebecca.

505
00:40:38,769 --> 00:40:40,896
[Rebecca] Ramon, fuck you! Let me go!

506
00:40:40,980 --> 00:40:42,106
[Ramon] Calm down!

507
00:40:43,357 --> 00:40:44,191
[gasps]

508
00:40:44,275 --> 00:40:46,068
- I don't want--
- Asshole, let my sister go!

509
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:47,069
[yelps]

510
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:50,197
- [Rebecca] Vedasto!
- [Ramon] Don't do it, Vedasto.

511
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:51,282
[whimpers]

512
00:40:51,365 --> 00:40:52,741
[Vedasto] You fucking piece of shit!

513
00:40:52,825 --> 00:40:54,743
Let my sister go!

514
00:40:57,830 --> 00:41:01,000
Yeah, yeah, keep squirming,
and I'll slit your neck.

515
00:41:01,083 --> 00:41:03,502
Is that something you understand, huh?

516
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:04,879
Get it, moron?

517
00:41:07,590 --> 00:41:08,424
Brother?

518
00:41:18,976 --> 00:41:20,519
Rebecca, run!

519
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:25,024
I'm older than you.

520
00:41:25,107 --> 00:41:27,401
When I say you have to go, then go!

521
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:31,447
Rebecca!

522
00:41:31,530 --> 00:41:32,573
I said go!

523
00:41:32,656 --> 00:41:35,493
I can't. [sobs]

524
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:53,719
- Don't come any closer-- [groans]
- Ah!

525
00:41:53,802 --> 00:41:55,012
[Javier panting]

526
00:41:56,430 --> 00:41:58,807
[Vedasto breathing heavily]

527
00:42:11,487 --> 00:42:12,696
[grunts]

528
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:19,870
[panting]

529
00:42:25,584 --> 00:42:27,253
[pants]

530
00:42:30,881 --> 00:42:33,425
[loud shrieking]

531
00:42:43,644 --> 00:42:45,396
[suspenseful music playing]

532
00:44:17,655 --> 00:44:19,740
[pants]

533
00:44:21,784 --> 00:44:22,660
[Crisanto] She went in.

534
00:44:25,287 --> 00:44:26,497
She's gone, Ramon

535
00:44:28,457 --> 00:44:29,375
[Ramon] Crisanto.

536
00:44:30,209 --> 00:44:31,752
Anyone ever gotten out of there?

537
00:44:33,545 --> 00:44:34,380
No one.

538
00:44:52,523 --> 00:44:54,817
This is all your fault, motherfucker.

539
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:56,944
This was none of your business.

540
00:44:57,986 --> 00:44:59,571
We were going to let your sister go.

541
00:45:04,410 --> 00:45:05,244
Don't shoot.

542
00:45:06,078 --> 00:45:07,538
It's too easy for him.

543
00:45:11,792 --> 00:45:14,711
No one touches these assholes
until I say so.

544
00:45:21,718 --> 00:45:23,679
You're allowed to live, Vedasto.

545
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:29,101
But your friends, though?

546
00:45:29,810 --> 00:45:32,062
I'm going to kill them very slowly,

547
00:45:32,146 --> 00:45:34,398
one by one, in front of you.

548
00:45:41,363 --> 00:45:42,489
You only die…

549
00:45:45,284 --> 00:45:47,411
when I say you die.

550
00:45:49,663 --> 00:45:51,707
You don't believe in the Lord, right?

551
00:45:58,589 --> 00:46:00,215
Well, now I am your Lord.

552
00:46:35,209 --> 00:46:37,961
[retches, coughs]

553
00:46:39,463 --> 00:46:41,590
[inhales sharply]

554
00:46:51,767 --> 00:46:54,228
[breathing heavily]

555
00:47:17,751 --> 00:47:19,002
[groans]

556
00:47:20,295 --> 00:47:22,589
[crickets chirping]

557
00:47:54,746 --> 00:47:57,749
[suspenseful music playing]

558
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:10,113
Hey, look. What is that?

559
00:49:13,533 --> 00:49:15,827
[fisherman 1] Oh, yeah.
She's dead, all right.

560
00:49:15,911 --> 00:49:17,704
- [fisherman 2] I wonder what happened.
- [sighs]

561
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:27,631
[suspenseful music playing]

562
00:49:34,888 --> 00:49:36,890
[coughs]

563
00:49:39,267 --> 00:49:40,352
[fisherman 2] She's still alive.

564
00:49:40,435 --> 00:49:41,645
- How can that be?
- [moans]

565
00:49:43,897 --> 00:49:47,150
[monitor beeps]

566
00:50:00,580 --> 00:50:01,415
[gasps]

567
00:50:02,165 --> 00:50:02,999
[sighs]

568
00:50:20,142 --> 00:50:21,184
[doctor] Ms. Tejeros.

569
00:50:25,147 --> 00:50:26,648
Doctor, where's my chain?

570
00:50:27,149 --> 00:50:27,983
We have it.

571
00:50:31,695 --> 00:50:33,280
How am I doing, doc?

572
00:50:33,363 --> 00:50:37,325
Well, the good news is,
your condition is stable now.

573
00:50:37,409 --> 00:50:40,662
I was worried because your fever
was very high the other day,

574
00:50:40,746 --> 00:50:42,038
but it's gone down now.

575
00:50:42,581 --> 00:50:44,624
There's no more water in your lungs,

576
00:50:44,708 --> 00:50:47,586
and all the small wounds you had

577
00:50:47,669 --> 00:50:49,713
have now completely healed.

578
00:50:51,673 --> 00:50:53,550
And you've regained consciousness.

579
00:50:56,928 --> 00:50:57,929
Is there bad news?

580
00:50:58,513 --> 00:50:59,514
That depends.

581
00:51:02,309 --> 00:51:03,393
Depends on?

582
00:51:05,312 --> 00:51:07,439
If you plan on having a child or not.

583
00:51:12,569 --> 00:51:14,488
You're pregnant, Ms. Tejeros.

584
00:51:16,573 --> 00:51:18,825
[officer] <i>That place you're talking about.</i>

585
00:51:19,451 --> 00:51:20,452
Well, there isn't--

586
00:51:21,119 --> 00:51:23,663
There just isn't any island mass
in that area,

587
00:51:23,747 --> 00:51:25,832
let alone an island that big.

588
00:51:26,792 --> 00:51:27,918
I was there.

589
00:51:29,961 --> 00:51:31,838
And I know my brother is still there.

590
00:51:31,922 --> 00:51:34,758
Uh, yes. Dr. Vedasto Tejeros.

591
00:51:35,675 --> 00:51:37,636
You were together on a research trip.

592
00:51:39,095 --> 00:51:41,681
There is a report, actually, that…

593
00:51:42,265 --> 00:51:46,478
uh, the local authorities lost contact
with the vessel's crew members.

594
00:51:47,020 --> 00:51:48,772
You're the only one that was found.

595
00:51:50,023 --> 00:51:50,857
They're alive.

596
00:51:52,359 --> 00:51:53,693
I know they are.

597
00:51:53,777 --> 00:51:55,028
My brother, the Cardomas.

598
00:51:55,654 --> 00:51:57,239
And they're not the only ones there, too.

599
00:51:57,864 --> 00:51:58,865
There are people.

600
00:51:58,949 --> 00:52:00,826
There are lots of other people.

601
00:52:06,331 --> 00:52:07,290
There was even--

602
00:52:11,962 --> 00:52:13,255
There was a man who…

603
00:52:14,381 --> 00:52:15,340
had bat wings.

604
00:52:17,592 --> 00:52:19,094
He had the wings of a bat.

605
00:52:21,137 --> 00:52:21,972
Bat wings.

606
00:52:26,852 --> 00:52:27,727
Shit.

607
00:52:28,854 --> 00:52:31,690
- Shit, shit, shit, shit.
- Miss, are you okay?

608
00:52:33,441 --> 00:52:35,402
Now I'm hearing my own story.

609
00:52:37,779 --> 00:52:39,239
I can't believe what I'm saying.

610
00:52:40,991 --> 00:52:42,284
Why would you believe me?

611
00:52:43,410 --> 00:52:44,911
But I'm not delirious.

612
00:52:45,745 --> 00:52:47,622
And I'm not making this up.

613
00:52:49,082 --> 00:52:52,794
And I understand you must think
I'm crazy and I'm wasting your time.

614
00:52:54,379 --> 00:52:57,549
Miss, you were reported missing
two weeks ago.

615
00:52:59,301 --> 00:53:01,678
You were picked up
in the middle of the ocean.

616
00:53:02,387 --> 00:53:03,471
You should be dead.

617
00:53:04,180 --> 00:53:06,558
But here you are, talking to me.

618
00:53:10,145 --> 00:53:11,521
So, are you new?

619
00:53:11,605 --> 00:53:13,064
I am. Yeah.

620
00:53:13,148 --> 00:53:15,650
I recently moved here from Sagay.

621
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:17,485
I just graduated. [chuckles]

622
00:53:18,069 --> 00:53:19,863
Uh, is it that obvious?

623
00:53:21,948 --> 00:53:24,534
That's why the police
are giving you the crazy ones?

624
00:53:25,577 --> 00:53:26,578
[scoffs]

625
00:53:27,829 --> 00:53:28,830
You know, miss,

626
00:53:29,623 --> 00:53:31,833
my gut's telling me you're not crazy.

627
00:53:34,628 --> 00:53:36,171
Sorry, what was your name again?

628
00:53:36,254 --> 00:53:38,340
Uh, Syquija, Ms. Tejeros.

629
00:53:38,840 --> 00:53:40,050
Arturo Syquija.

630
00:53:40,634 --> 00:53:42,928
[singing] <i>♪ Dandansoy ♪</i>

631
00:53:43,011 --> 00:53:44,471
<i>♪ My young dear ♪</i>

632
00:53:44,554 --> 00:53:46,097
<i>♪ I'm afraid ♪</i>

633
00:53:46,181 --> 00:53:48,850
<i>♪ I have to leave you now ♪</i>

634
00:53:48,934 --> 00:53:51,728
<i>♪ I'll go back to Payao ♪</i>

635
00:53:52,604 --> 00:53:54,147
<i>♪ Though I yearn for ♪</i>

636
00:53:55,690 --> 00:53:56,816
"Sabrina," huh?

637
00:53:57,484 --> 00:53:59,486
I can't believe
they spelled it incorrectly.

638
00:54:00,070 --> 00:54:01,237
It's the right spelling.

639
00:54:01,821 --> 00:54:03,907
- Maybe read it as written.
- Yeah.

640
00:54:04,658 --> 00:54:06,785
It's Sabina, no R.

641
00:54:06,868 --> 00:54:08,411
Oh, shit. Sabina.

642
00:54:08,495 --> 00:54:09,329
Very fancy.

643
00:54:09,412 --> 00:54:11,289
[shushes] Don't swear
in front of your goddaughter.

644
00:54:11,373 --> 00:54:12,248
Sorry.

645
00:54:14,668 --> 00:54:15,502
Goddaughter?

646
00:54:16,086 --> 00:54:17,337
You can't say no.

647
00:54:18,755 --> 00:54:20,298
Don't I get a choice here?

648
00:54:20,382 --> 00:54:22,676
Like I had a choice?
You're the only one I know here.

649
00:54:23,635 --> 00:54:25,095
Well, it looks like we're even.

650
00:54:25,178 --> 00:54:27,847
[Sabina crying]

651
00:54:27,931 --> 00:54:28,932
She's cute.

652
00:54:29,015 --> 00:54:29,975
She looks like you.

653
00:54:31,851 --> 00:54:35,563
- [Sabina babbling]
- [Arturo] Here.

654
00:54:37,607 --> 00:54:40,110
[Sabina singing]

655
00:54:46,449 --> 00:54:47,617
I'm starting to think,

656
00:54:49,119 --> 00:54:50,328
if there is a God,

657
00:54:52,497 --> 00:54:54,624
then Sabina is His way

658
00:54:55,583 --> 00:54:57,502
of saying sorry for Vedasto.

659
00:55:00,839 --> 00:55:04,467
If there's a God, I think
He's more complicated than that.

660
00:55:04,551 --> 00:55:06,094
God isn't complicated.

661
00:55:09,931 --> 00:55:11,683
People, yes. God, no

662
00:55:17,105 --> 00:55:19,441
How long before I can let my brother go?

663
00:55:26,698 --> 00:55:27,949
It's been years,

664
00:55:28,033 --> 00:55:30,118
but I know that he's still alive.

665
00:55:33,204 --> 00:55:34,372
At least, I hope he is.

666
00:55:39,044 --> 00:55:42,047
If I can get Vedasto home,
maybe he'll meet his niece.

667
00:55:44,215 --> 00:55:46,176
My brother's had my back my whole life.

668
00:55:47,177 --> 00:55:48,845
I've never done anything for him.

669
00:55:49,971 --> 00:55:51,890
But where will you start, Rebecca?

670
00:55:53,808 --> 00:55:54,851
Aren't you a cop?

671
00:55:56,478 --> 00:55:57,353
You tell me.

672
00:56:31,638 --> 00:56:32,514
[Arturo groans]

673
00:56:35,850 --> 00:56:38,853
[suspenseful music playing]

674
00:56:48,655 --> 00:56:50,406
[Sabina] <i>Why didn't you tell me</i>
<i>all of this before?</i>

675
00:56:52,158 --> 00:56:53,493
Would you have believed me?

676
00:56:53,576 --> 00:56:55,078
I would have tried to understand.

677
00:56:55,161 --> 00:56:57,413
You never would have let me out, Sabina.

678
00:56:57,497 --> 00:56:59,999
You would have trussed me up
so I couldn't go anywhere.

679
00:57:00,083 --> 00:57:00,917
I know you.

680
00:57:01,000 --> 00:57:02,710
- I wouldn't--
- Tell me I'm wrong.

681
00:57:02,794 --> 00:57:04,087
[sighs]

682
00:57:05,630 --> 00:57:06,464
I'm not.

683
00:57:08,133 --> 00:57:09,759
I didn't tell you anything,

684
00:57:09,843 --> 00:57:13,179
and yet you still managed
to track me down.

685
00:57:14,722 --> 00:57:16,099
You shouldn't have followed me.

686
00:57:17,058 --> 00:57:18,476
Well, we're here now.

687
00:57:18,560 --> 00:57:20,228
Let's just focus on getting back again.

688
00:57:21,813 --> 00:57:23,523
[groans]

689
00:57:24,274 --> 00:57:25,108
What is it?

690
00:57:25,775 --> 00:57:26,860
- [groans in pain]
- Ma!

691
00:57:27,444 --> 00:57:28,278
Ma!

692
00:57:28,361 --> 00:57:30,196
[Rebecca groans]

693
00:57:31,448 --> 00:57:32,490
[muted groan]

694
00:57:32,574 --> 00:57:34,325
- [groans]
- Ma!

695
00:57:42,250 --> 00:57:44,502
[both panting]

696
00:57:44,586 --> 00:57:45,587
Just try to walk.

697
00:57:45,670 --> 00:57:47,380
[Rebecca pants]

698
00:57:51,676 --> 00:57:52,844
Is this where it is?

699
00:57:54,596 --> 00:57:56,514
Yes. The boat, it's over there.

700
00:57:59,767 --> 00:58:01,311
[groaning]

701
00:58:04,606 --> 00:58:06,566
Ma, let's go home.

702
00:58:06,649 --> 00:58:08,568
I'll return later for Bulak and Uncle Art.

703
00:58:08,651 --> 00:58:09,819
- No, wait.
- Later.

704
00:58:16,784 --> 00:58:17,619
[sighs]

705
00:58:18,369 --> 00:58:21,539
[Diwa chokes]

706
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:25,043
[groans]

707
00:58:25,919 --> 00:58:26,753
[gasps]

708
00:58:27,670 --> 00:58:29,631
[snarling]

709
00:58:38,431 --> 00:58:40,183
[screams]

710
00:58:55,365 --> 00:58:57,367
[screams louder]

711
00:58:59,953 --> 00:59:02,956
[closing theme music playing]
